## DeepSeek Harness (`@deepseek-ai/*`, MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 DeepSeek)

The following adapted material is derived from the installed DSH 0.2.1-rc.2
package `@deepseek-ai/dsh-compaction-basic` (and, for the preset copy,
`@deepseek-ai/dsh-web-app`):

- `src/budget.js` — the pressure/threshold/retention formulas from
  `resolveCompactSpec` and the specification/selection rules from
  `resolveTargetPolicy` and `selectCompactableRange`. The DSH build is bundled;
  these functions are not exported from the package, so the formulas are
  re-implemented in one clearly marked adapter module and must stay
  behavior-compatible with the native engine. Changed: TypeScript types were
  dropped, diagnostics were reworded, and the functions take detached plain
  configuration.
- `src/engine.js` — the shape of the one-shot summarization request (replayed
  prefix, final user instruction, `purpose: 'compaction'`, assembler and
  fail-closed finish mapping) follows `summarizeWithLlm` / `summarizeCompaction`
  so goal and handoff summaries reuse the native warm prefix instead of copying
  the whole native engine. Changed: the instruction text and structured output
  are new; reasoning-effort/cache-priority handling and output structure
  validation are added.
- `presets/better-compact.patch.yml` — a verbatim copy of
  `@deepseek-ai/dsh-web-app@0.2.1-rc.2` `presets/standard.patch.yml` with exactly
  one row (`compaction-basic` → `dsh-better-compact/engine`) and the preset
  identity/metadata changed. The original copyright and MIT license apply.

The native checkpoint preamble and `<compacted-summary>` framing text are
reproduced in `src/inspect.js` **only** to price the preview's replacement upper
bound (`NATIVE_CHECKPOINT_FRAMING_TOKENS`); native mode itself still calls the
inherited `summarize()` implementation, so the installed host remains the only
source of the actual framing written to a checkpoint.

## Design references (no source copied)

The goal/handoff prompt structure and the inspection contract were informed by
the public design documents and by fixed-version review of MIT/Apache-2.0
projects (pi-atlas, xbot, OpenCode V2, Codex). No substantial source code or
prompt text from those projects is included here; they are research references,
not runtime dependencies, and this repository does not claim their quality or
behavior.
